╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that in rtl/ibex_register_file_fpga.sv, signals       │
│ oh_raddr_a_err and oh_raddr_b_err are only driven inside the if    │
│ (RdataMuxCheck) generate block.                                    │
│ When RdataMuxCheck == 0, that block is not elaborated, so both     │
│ signals become undriven, and err_o (which depends on them)         │
│ references undriven logic. Verilator correctly flags this as       │
│ UNDRIVEN.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In ibex_register_file_fpga.sv:                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Declaration/use:                                                │
│     • logic oh_raddr_a_err, oh_raddr_b_err, oh_we_err;             │
│     • assign err_o = oh_raddr_a_err || oh_raddr_b_err ||           │
│       oh_we_err;                                                   │
│  • oh_raddr_a_err/oh_raddr_b_err are assigned only in              │
│    gen_rdata_mux_check (if (RdataMuxCheck) branch), but not in     │
│    gen_no_rdata_mux_check (else) branch.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Ensure every internal signal that contributes to outputs is     │
│    driven in all generate/elaboration configurations.              │
│  • Prefer explicit tie-offs (1'b0) when optional checks are        │
│    disabled.                                                       │
│  • Keep behavior unchanged for enabled security checks; only       │
│    remove undriven conditions when disabled.                       │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Add explicit assignments in gen_no_rdata_mux_check:                │
│                                                                    │
│  • assign oh_raddr_a_err = 1'b0;                                   │
│  • assign oh_raddr_b_err = 1'b0;                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps err_o well-defined and lint-clean when RdataMuxCheck is │
│ disabled, while preserving existing behavior when enabled.         │
│                                                                    │
