First, we need to make sure that “debug mode” actually turns off the instruction‐cache enable flags all the way down in the front end.  If you look at how Ibex carries debug status through from the CSR block into the fetch stage and then into the I$ block, you can see where the extra gating needs to happen:

1. In csr.sv we have to expose the debug‐mode bit (DCSR[DMODE]) properly.  
2. In the top‐level core (ibex_core.sv) we need to hook that debug bit into the fetch stage.  
3. In the fetch_stage (fetch_stage.sv) we need to gate the normal icache‐enable signals off when debug is active.  
4. In the icache implementation (icache.sv) we also have to make sure that we never launch any real “cache” transactions when debug is true (bypass or hold‐off).

Those four files are therefore the primary touchpoints for disabling I$ in debug mode.

```  
hw/ip/ibex_pr81/rtl/csr.sv  
hw/ip/ibex_pr81/rtl/ibex_core.sv  
hw/ip/ibex_pr81/rtl/fetch_stage.sv  
hw/ip/ibex_pr81/rtl/icache.sv  
```
