│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ For CMO_PREFETCH with prefetch_updt_plru == 1, PLRU update         │
│ behavior is inconsistent:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • On prefetch hit: PLRU is not updated.                           │
│  • On prefetch miss/refill: PLRU is updated (via refill path).     │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • In hpdcache_miss_handler.sv, PLRU update on refill is           │
│    explicitly enabled for prefetch when                            │
│    cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i is set:                          │
│     • refill_updt_sel_victim_o = ~refill_is_error_o &              │
│       (~is_prefetch | cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i);             │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl.sv, CMO_PREFETCH is decoded as CMO prefetch,   │
│    but not load-like in stage decode (st0_req_is_load /            │
│    st1_req_is_load).                                               │
│    Hit-path PLRU update logic is typically tied to load/store hit  │
│    classification, so prefetch hits do not trigger it.             │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep change minimal and localized to request classification.    │
│  • Preserve existing miss/refill behavior.                         │
│  • Avoid protocol/FSM rewrites.                                    │
│  • Keep decode behavior consistent across stage 0 and stage 1.     │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Make CMO_PREFETCH decode as load-like for internal control         │
│ classification in both stage 0 and stage 1:                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • st*_req_is_load = is_load(op) | is_cmo_prefetch(op);            │
│                                                                    │
│ This enables prefetch hits to follow the load-like hit path        │
│ (including PLRU update behavior), matching miss-side behavior when │
│ prefetch PLRU updates are enabled.                                 │
