│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue reports inconsistent PLRU behavior for CMO_PREFETCH when │
│ prefetch_updt_plru == 1:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • On prefetch hit: PLRU is not updated.                           │
│  • On prefetch miss: PLRU is updated on refill response.           │
│                                                                    │
│ This creates asymmetric replacement-state behavior for the same    │
│ request type.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided context, the miss-side PLRU update is explicitly │
│ controlled in rtl/src/hpdcache_miss_handler.sv:                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • In REFILL_WRITE:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│     refill_updt_sel_victim_o  =  ~refill_is_error_o &              │
│                                 (~is_prefetch |                    │
│     cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i);                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • In REFILL_WRITE_DIR:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│     refill_updt_sel_victim_o  = ~refill_is_error_o &               │
│                                (~refill_is_prefetch_q |            │
│     cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i);                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ These conditions allow prefetch misses to update PLRU (when cfg is │
│ enabled), while hit-path behavior remains non-updating, causing    │
│ inconsistency.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior consistent for the same operation class           │
│    (CMO_PREFETCH) across hit/miss outcomes.                        │
│  • Minimize RTL impact and avoid protocol-side side effects.       │
│  • Preserve existing error gating (~refill_is_error_o).            │
│  • Avoid broad semantic changes (e.g., reclassifying prefetch as   │
│    load globally).                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Apply a minimal fix in miss handler so refill path no longer       │
│ updates victim selection for prefetches.                           │
│ This aligns miss behavior with current hit behavior and removes    │
│ inconsistency.                                                     │
