│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is about CMO prefetch (HPDCACHE_REQ_CMO_PREFETCH)        │
│ behavior with prefetch_updt_plru == 1:                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • On miss: PLRU gets updated (in refill path).                    │
│  • On hit: PLRU is not updated.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So behavior is inconsistent between hit and miss for prefetch      │
│ traffic.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided code:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • In hpdcache_miss_handler.sv, PLRU/victim update on refill is    │
│    explicitly controlled for prefetches:                           │
│                                                                    │
│     refill_updt_sel_victim_o = ~refill_is_error_o &                │
│                                (~is_prefetch |                     │
│     cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i);                               │
│                                                                    │
│    So prefetch miss path already supports configurable update.     │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl.sv, prefetch is decoded separately             │
│    (st*_req_is_cmo_prefetch) and not treated as load in            │
│    st*_req_is_load. Hit-side PLRU update logic typically follows   │
│    load/use semantics, so prefetch hit does not participate.       │
│  • Also, hpdcache_ctrl does not currently expose a prefetch-PLRU   │
│    config input in its config port list.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep change minimal and localized.                              │
│  • Reuse existing config intent (cfg_prefetch_updt_plru) so        │
│    behavior is controllable.                                       │
│  • Avoid changing non-prefetch op behavior.                        │
│  • Avoid broad semantic changes in miss handler/refill FSM         │
│    (already correct for miss).                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add a config input in hpdcache_ctrl for prefetch-hit PLRU       │
│    update control.                                                 │
│  • Make prefetch requests count as load-like accesses in           │
│    stage0/stage1 decode only when config is enabled.               │
│  • Use 4-state-safe comparison (=== 1'b1) to avoid X/Z propagation │
│    if unconnected in some integration.                             │
│                                                                    │
