I looked at where the PMP address register (`pmp_addr_rdata`) is declared (in the CSR‐registers RTL) and where it gets hooked up to the RVFI port (in the `cv32e40s_wrapper`).  These two must agree, and currently one is `PMP_ADDR_WIDTH` bits wide while the RVFI port is fixed at 32 bits.  You therefore need to either change the CSR declaration (or its parameter) or adjust the wrapper’s port (or both).  You will also need to update the common parameter file where `PMP_ADDR_WIDTH` is defined so it defaults to 32 bits, and the RVFI package definition to keep everything in sync.

```
// 1) The behavioral wrapper that defines the RVFI port and hooks up pmp_addr_rdata
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv

// 2) The CSR‐registers RTL where pmp_addr_rdata is declared
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/rtl/cs_registers.sv

// 3) The parameter file that defines PMP_ADDR_WIDTH
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/rtl/parameters.sv

// 4) The RVFI/UVM package that declares the RVFI pmp‐address port width
sim/uvmt/vsrc/uvmt_cv32e40s_pkg.sv
```
