Based on the fact that the execute‐permission enforcement for “no matching PMP region + MML=1” must live in the PMP checker but also needs to be surfaced to IFU via the CSR interface, the four places to touch are:

  1. The main PMP‐checker itself (where we actually decide “no region + MML => deny X”)
  2. The IFU (so that denied‐X trips an IF‐page‐fault rather than returning the instruction)
  3. The MSECCFG CSR definition (to expose the MML bit)
  4. The PMP‐CSR glue (so writes to MSECCFG/pmpcfg are hooked up to the PMP checker)

```text
rtl/core/pmp/cv32e40s_pmp.sv
rtl/core/ifu/cv32e40s_ifu.sv
rtl/core/csr/cv32e40s_mseccfg.sv
rtl/core/pmp/cv32e40s_pmp_csr.sv
```
