│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The PMP/Smepmp behavior is incorrect when mseccfg.MML=1 and no PMP │
│ region matches an instruction fetch in M-mode.                     │
│ Current RTL allows the fetch (default allow in M-mode when         │
│ MMWP=0), but Smepmp requires execute to be denied in this case.    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in rtl/cv32e40s_pmp.sv, in the access fault           │
│ prioritization default logic:                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • access_fault is initialized as:                                 │
│     • deny if MMWP=1                                               │
│     • otherwise allow in M-mode / deny in S/U-mode                 │
│  • This default does not account for MML=1 execute requests with   │
│    no matching rule.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ So with no matching PMP entry:                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • MMWP=0, priv_lvl_i==M, pmp_req_type_i==EXEC, MML=1              │
│  • current default becomes allow (access_fault=0) → wrong.         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep fix minimal and local to PMP decision logic.               │
│  • Preserve existing matching-rule priority behavior.              │
│  • Only adjust default no-match policy for the specific Smepmp     │
│    case.                                                           │
│  • Do not alter unrelated CSR or IF-stage flow.                    │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ In access_fault default assignment, add the Smepmp-specific        │
│ condition:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • If MML=1 and request type is EXEC, default to deny              │
│    (access_fault=1) before applying region-match overrides.        │
│  • Keep existing MMWP / privilege behavior for other cases.        │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • No-match execute is denied when MML=1.                          │
│  • Matching PMP entries still determine final permission via       │
│    existing priority loop.                                         │
│                                                                    │
