│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that after setting mseccfg.MML=1 (with no PMP entries │
│ configured), the core still allows fetching/executing the next     │
│ instruction in M-mode.                                             │
│ Per Smepmp, when MML=1, executing from an address with no matching │
│ PMP rule must be denied.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ So the bug is a wrong default permission for instruction fetch in  │
│ M-mode when no PMP region matches and MML=1.                       │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in rtl/cv32e40s_pmp.sv, in the access fault           │
│ prioritization default assignment:                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  access_fault = csr_pmp_i.mseccfg.mmwp || (priv_lvl_i !=           │
│  PRIV_LVL_M);                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This default allows unmatched accesses in M-mode when MMWP=0,      │
│ regardless of MML.                                                 │
│ Since the fetch path can have no matching region immediately after │
│ setting MML, instruction fetch incorrectly passes.                 │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior unchanged for non-MML scenarios.                  │
│  • Apply the narrowest fix: only change default behavior required  │
│    by spec.                                                        │
│  • Let existing region-priority/override logic remain intact.      │
│  • Keep combinational logic simple and deterministic.              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Change default access_fault logic so that when:                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • mseccfg.MML=1, and                                              │
│  • request is instruction fetch (PMP_ACC_EXEC),                    │
