│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The core currently allows the next instruction fetch in M-mode     │
│ right after mseccfg.MML is set, when no PMP region matches.        │
│ Per Smepmp, with MML=1, execution from memory without a matching   │
│ PMP rule must be denied (and also denied for matching S/U-only     │
│ rules in M-mode).                                                  │
│ So the default “no matching rule” behavior for instruction fetch   │
│ is wrong.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
