539   // csr_op_en_o is set when CSR access should actually happen.
540   // csv_access_o is set when CSR access instruction is present and is used to compute whether a CSR
541   // access is illegal. A combinational loop would be created if csr_op_en_o was used along (as
542   // asserting it for an illegal csr access would result in a flush that would need to deassert it).
543   assign csr_op_en_o             = csr_access_o & instr_executing & instr_id_done_o;
