816   // When writeback stage is present RVFI information is emitted when instruction is finished in
817   // third stage but some information must be captured whilst the instruction is in the second
818   // stage. Without writeback stage RVFI information is all emitted when instruction retires in
819   // second stage. RVFI outputs are all straight from flops. So 2 stage pipeline requires a single
820   // set of flops (instr_info => RVFI_out), 3 stage pipeline requires two sets (instr_info => wb
821   // => RVFI_out)
