│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_lite_mux declares axi_req_t and axi_resp_t as type parameters  │
│ defaulting to logic.                                               │
│ Inside the module, these types are used as structs (.aw,           │
│ .aw_valid, .w, etc.).                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ Some simulators tolerate this until instantiation overrides the    │
│ types. XSim instead errors early when parsing/elaborating those    │
│ member accesses against the default logic type.                    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/axi_lite_mux.sv, parameter defaults are:                    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  parameter type axi_req_t  = logic,                                │
│  parameter type axi_resp_t = logic,                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ but later code accesses:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  slv_reqs_i[i].aw                                                  │
│  slv_reqs_i[i].aw_valid                                            │
│  slv_resps_o[i].aw_ready                                           │
│  ...                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So the defaults are structurally incompatible with module          │
│ internals.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Provide structurally valid default type parameters for generic  │
│    modules.                                                        │
│  • Make defaults self-consistent with other channel type           │
│    parameters (aw_chan_t, w_chan_t, etc.).                         │
│  • Avoid tool-dependent behavior (deferred type checking           │
│    differences across simulators).                                 │
│  • Keep changes minimal and backward-compatible for users who      │
│    already override types.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Replace axi_req_t and axi_resp_t defaults with packed struct       │
│ defaults matching AXI-Lite request/response field definitions      │
│ (same fields used in the module).                                  │
│ This keeps existing explicit overrides working while making the    │
│ module compile robustly even when wrappers forget to pass these    │
│ two type params.                                                   │
