│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_lite_mux is parameterized with channel types (aw_chan_t,       │
│ w_chan_t, etc.) and also full request/response types (axi_req_t,   │
│ axi_resp_t).                                                       │
│ In at least one instantiation path (as you noticed for             │
│ axi_lite_mux_intf), axi_req_t and axi_resp_t are not explicitly    │
│ passed, so they fall back to their defaults (logic).               │
│                                                                    │
│ Then code like:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • slv_reqs_i[i].aw                                                │
│  • slv_reqs_i[i].aw_valid                                          │
│  • slv_resps_o[i].aw_ready                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ fails, because logic has no struct fields.                         │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/axi_lite_mux.sv, the type parameter defaults are currently: │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  parameter type axi_req_t  = logic,                                │
│  parameter type axi_resp_t = logic,                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ while the module body assumes AXI-Lite struct fields exist         │
│ (AW/W/AR channels + valid/ready signals).                          │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best-practice considerations                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Type parameter defaults should be self-consistent with how they │
│    are used in the module.                                         │
│  • If request/response types are derivable from channel type       │
│    parameters, defaults should be derived from those channel types │
│    rather than logic.                                              │
│  • Keep backwards compatibility: explicit type overrides should    │
│    still work unchanged.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Change default definitions of axi_req_t and axi_resp_t from logic  │
│ to AXI-Lite-compatible packed structs constructed from the channel │
│ type parameters.                                                   │
│ This makes the module robust even when an instantiation forgets to │
│ pass axi_req_t / axi_resp_t (as in your XSim case), while          │
│ preserving normal explicit typing flows.                           │
