│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_lite_mux_intf instantiates axi_lite_mux without explicitly     │
│ passing axi_req_t / axi_resp_t.                                    │
│ In axi_lite_mux, these type parameters currently default to logic, │
│ but inside the module they are used as structs (slv_reqs_i[i].aw,  │
│ .w_valid, etc.).                                                   │
│ With XSim, this causes compile-time errors like “aw is not         │
│ declared under prefix slv_reqs_i”.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is in src/axi_lite_mux.sv parameter defaults:       │
│                                                                    │
│  • parameter type axi_req_t = logic                                │
│  • parameter type axi_resp_t = logic                               │
│                                                                    │
│ These defaults are incompatible with internal field access in the  │
│ module.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep backward compatibility: explicit user-provided axi_req_t / │
│    axi_resp_t should still work.                                   │
│  • Make defaults self-consistent with other channel type           │
│    parameters.                                                     │
│  • Avoid forcing every wrapper/interface instantiation to pass     │
│    redundant type params.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Change the defaults of axi_req_t and axi_resp_t from logic to      │
│ packed struct defaults derived from aw_chan_t, w_chan_t, b_chan_t, │
│ ar_chan_t, and r_chan_t (matching AXI-Lite typedef layout).        │
│ This makes the module compile correctly even when those two type   │
