│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that atomic AXI operations (RISC-V AMOs/ATOPs) are    │
│ not handled on the path to the L2 SPM.                             │
│ Cheshire already inserts axi_riscv_atomics_structs in front of its │
│ internal memories/slave ports, but carfield still needs this       │
│ conversion in front of its own L2 SPM ports.                       │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided context in hw/carfield.sv, the L2 ports are      │
│ exposed as external AXI slaves (L2Port1SlvIdx, L2Port2SlvIdx from  │
│ carfield_pkg.sv), but there is no visible atomic adapter wiring    │
│ for those L2 paths in the shown top-level integration area.        │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant integration/declaration area is around:               │
│                                                                    │
│  • AXI/local interconnect signal declarations                      │
│  • “Mailbox unit” declarations                                     │
│  • “Carfield IPs” integration section (where IP-level wiring is    │
│    assembled)                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the patch minimal and localized to top-level integration.  │
│  • Insert axi_riscv_atomics_structs only on L2 SPM ingress paths   │
│    (L2Port1/L2Port2).                                              │
│  • Preserve existing AXI typing (carfield_axi_slv_req_t/rsp_t) and │
│    avoid changing address maps or slave indices.                   │
│  • Keep clock/reset consistent with the target memory domain (L2   │
│    domain reset/clock already present in the module).              │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add intermediate AXI req/rsp signals for L2 ports (host-side    │
│    and memory-side around the atomics adapter).                    │
│  • Instantiate two axi_riscv_atomics_structs blocks, one per L2    │
│    SPM AXI port.                                                   │
│  • Route L2 external slave traffic through those wrappers before   │
│    reaching L2 SPM.                                                │
