│  1 Problem statement                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ The current stream_join behavior (as described in the issue) is    │
│ too strict:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • it always joins all inputs,                                     │
│  • and it only grants handshakes when all selected inputs are      │
│    valid in the same cycle.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ Requested behavior is a dynamic-join variant that:                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • supports a per-transaction selection mask (join only a subset), │
│  • allows independent input handshakes (inputs can handshake in    │
│    different cycles), while still producing one joined output      │
│    event once all selected inputs have handshaked.                 │
│                                                                    │
