│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem statement                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ The current stream_join behavior is static and strict:             │
│                                                                    │
│  • It always joins all input streams.                              │
│  • It only grants input ready when all selected inputs are valid   │
│    in the same cycle (simultaneous input handshakes).              │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue requests a dynamic variant that:                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • supports a runtime selection mask (join only a subset),         │
│  • allows independent input handshakes (inputs can handshake in    │
│    different cycles).                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the problem occurs                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The missing functionality is conceptual in the join/fork handshake │
│ family.                                                            │
│ From the provided context, stream_fork already implements          │
│ “independent branch handshakes over time” semantics, and there is  │
│ already a stream_fork_dynamic in the repository list.              │
│ So the cleanest fix is to provide a dynamic join module as the     │
│ mirror (“specular”) of dynamic fork behavior.                      │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep existing IPs backward-compatible (stream_join unchanged).  │
│  • Add a new IP (stream_join_dynamic) instead of altering existing │
│    semantics.                                                      │
│  • Reuse proven logic by structural composition (instantiate       │
│    stream_fork_dynamic) rather than duplicating complex state      │
│    logic.                                                          │
│  • Preserve parameter guards (N_INP >= 1 assertion).               │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Add stream_join_dynamic as a mirror wrapper around                 │
│ stream_fork_dynamic:                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Map join single output side to fork single input side by        │
│    swapping valid/ready roles appropriately.                       │
│  • Expose selection mask sel_i for dynamic subset joins.           │
│  • This naturally enables independent per-input handshakes while   │
│    still completing one combined output transaction.               │
