Based on the description, the violation is caused by always tying both ExtPrio=1 and LockIn=1 when ARBITER="prio" in the stream‐arbiter files, which then trips the assertion inside rr_arb_tree. To fix this you’ll need to:

 1. Change the instantiation inside src/stream_arbiter_flushable.sv so that LockIn isn’t set together with ExtPrio when ARBITER="prio".
 2. Do the same in src/stream_arbiter.sv.
 3. Potentially update the assertion or parameter checking in src/rr_arb_tree.sv to either relax or more clearly document the allowed combinations.

