│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ stream_arbiter_flushable (and therefore stream_arbiter) configures │
│ rr_arb_tree in "prio" mode with:                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • ExtPrio = 1'b1                                                  │
│  • LockIn  = 1'b1                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ But rr_arb_tree has a built-in assertion that explicitly forbids   │
│ this combination:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assert(!(LockIn && ExtPrio))                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So any "prio" instantiation triggers a fatal assertion.            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • In src/stream_arbiter_flushable.sv, in gen_prio_arb, the        │
│    rr_arb_tree instantiation sets both ExtPrio and LockIn to 1'b1. │
│  • src/stream_arbiter.sv wraps stream_arbiter_flushable, so it     │
│    inherits this issue.                                            │
│  • Assertion is in src/rr_arb_tree.sv initial checks.              │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Respect callee module parameter constraints (rr_arb_tree        │
│    contract).                                                      │
│  • Make minimal changes with no interface/API breakage.            │
│  • Keep behavior selection ("rr" vs "prio") intact.                │
│  • Avoid invasive refactors unless strictly necessary.             │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ For "prio" mode in stream_arbiter_flushable, set:                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • LockIn from 1'b1 to 1'b0                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ This makes the parameter combination legal (ExtPrio=1, LockIn=0)   │
│ and removes the inherent fatal assertion.                          │
