I focused on how the interleaving address bits are computed and stripped. The main work happens in the multi‐bank SRAM wrapper (`l2_ram_multibank.sv`), in the per‐bank address mux, and in the overall L2 memory top/interconnect that instantiates and wires up the banked SRAM. Those four files are where the extraction of “word­offset” vs “bank­offset” must be updated to drop not only the 2 LSBs (for 32-bit words) but also the `$clog2(NUM_BANKS)` bank-select bits.

```  
hw/rtl/memory/l2_ram_multibank.sv  
hw/rtl/memory/l2_bank_mux.sv  
hw/rtl/memory/l2_controller.sv  
hw/rtl/interconnect/axi_l2_interconnect.sv  
```
