│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that when trst_ni is asserted low, the TAP state      │
│ machine is being reset to RunTestIdle, but according to IEEE       │
│ 1149.1 the TAP controller must reset to Test-Logic-Reset.          │
│                                                                    │
│ So the current reset behavior is incorrect for JTAG TAP state      │
│ handling.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in src/dmi_jtag_tap.sv, inside the sequential TAP state │
│ register update block:                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • Location #2 / #3                                                │
│                                                                    │
│     always_ff @(posedge tck_i or negedge trst_ni) begin : p_regs   │
│       if (!trst_ni) begin                                          │
│         tap_state_q <= RunTestIdle;                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This is the state reset assignment that must be changed.           │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Follow the IEEE 1149.1 TAP reset semantics: asynchronous reset  │
│    should bring the TAP to TestLogicReset.                         │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Do not alter unrelated reset behavior for idcode_q or bypass_q  │
│    unless needed.                                                  │
│  • Ensure the TAP state machine’s reset state is consistent with   │
│    the combinational FSM logic and with test_logic_reset           │
│    signaling.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Change the reset assignment of tap_state_q from RunTestIdle to     │
│ TestLogicReset in the asynchronous reset branch of the TAP         │
