│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is not really a typo in the comments; it is a mismatch   │
│ in the generated abstract command sequence for the AccessRegister  │
│ command when HasSndScratch is enabled.                             │
│                                                                    │
│ In the a0 access path, the code currently does this:               │
│                                                                    │
│  • saves a0 into dscratch1 at the start of the abstract command    │
│  • later, when it needs a0 as a temporary to form the Debug Module │
│    address, it tries to use a0 again                               │
│  • the question is whether a0 needs to be restored from dscratch1  │
│    before the abstract command, or whether that restore is         │
│    unnecessary                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The key point is:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • a0 and dscratch1 are not inherently “the same”.                 │
│  • dscratch1 is just a storage location used to preserve the       │
│    original a0.                                                    │
│  • The abstract command uses a0 as a scratch register internally,  │
│    so it may overwrite it.                                         │
│  • Therefore, the sequence must preserve and restore a0 when       │
│    needed.                                                         │
