│  • as a result, the macros AXI_FLATTEN_MASTER and                  │
│    AXI_FLATTEN_SLAVE are undefined                                 │
│  • synthesis stops when compiling occamy_xilinx.sv                 │
│                                                                    │
│ So the issue is not in the AXI logic itself, but in the missing    │
│ macro definitions needed to flatten AXI structs into port signals. │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problem appears in hw/system/occamy/src/occamy_xilinx.sv at:   │
│                                                                    │
│  • the include directive:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│     `include "axi_flat.svh"                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • and later where the missing macros are used:                    │
│                                                                    │
│     `AXI_FLATTEN_MASTER(...)                                       │
│     `AXI_FLATTEN_SLAVE(...)                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ If the included file is absent, both the include and macro         │
│ expansion fail.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Minimal change: only fix the missing dependency issue, do not   │
