Based on the description, the signals `we_al` and `be_al` are mis-declared as single bits in the Xilinx-specific SRAM “tech-cell” (only the first byte ever gets enabled), and the generic latch stage also needs to pass thru the full byte-enable vector.  In particular you will need to fix:

1) The Xilinx-wrapper module that instantiates the BRAM primitive and latches address/control (`we_al`, `be_al`) – it currently declares those ports as 1-bit instead of N-bits.  
2) The generic SRAM latch module so that the full `be` bus is captured into `be_al` (and likewise for `we_al`).  
3) The lower-level Xilinx BRAM instantiation file (where the primitive’s WEA port is connected) to pass the full byte-enable width.  
4) The Xilinx testbench so that it actually drives and checks all bytes, not just byte-0.

The four files you should edit are:

```  
cells/fpgas/xilinx/tc_sram_xilinx.sv  
cells/common/tc_sram_generic.sv  
cells/fpgas/xilinx/ram_1p_1w_32b_xilinx.sv  
tests/tc_sram_xilinx.sv  
```
